{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:58:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:58:31+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:58:34+02:00\nThe search for \"\"Bounds on Roman domination numbers of graphs\" \"Mobaraky\" \"Sheikholeslami\" \"diameter\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe paper **\"Bounds on Roman domination numbers of graphs\"** by **B.P. Mobaraky** and **S.M. Sheikholeslami** was published in the journal ***Matematički Vesnik***, Volume 60, Issue 4, in **2008** (pages 247–253)[1][2][3].\n\n### Summary of the Paper\n*   **Topic:** The authors investigate the Roman domination number ($\\gamma_R(G)$) of a graph $G$[1][4].\n*   **Key Results:** The paper provides **lower and upper bounds** for the Roman domination number in terms of fundamental graph parameters, specifically the **diameter** and the **girth** of the graph[1][5]. \n*   **Specific Finding:** For example, the paper establishes that if a graph $G$ has a diameter of two, then $\\gamma_R(G)$ is bounded by a specific value[6].\n\nThis work is frequently cited in subsequent research regarding Roman domination in graph theory[7][8][9], including studies that later improved these bounds for specific classes of graphs (such as graphs with a minimum degree $\\delta(G) \\geq 2$)[10][5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [researchgate.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEYU-NJRA_hr5XlADzJIKCcGtBL9LVYOogmN2lweUQY01Bh3RsTysAbFW_qPqjFoBMKUjvZhjtR78TD2VUz2kcRSvjDfS7zaZAyeqy7K0j44VMKNxRp7_vnIJ_6SvkQt96NNs6AxJ7PUh1t5IHBZ-Wk9eQNz83wmxCW4jdiXvQPQ38aGfWkR0Q90JoWsZjT9QmLXQANow==)\n[2] [math.rs](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG7S-PYA9cfmMRG8JAgSoy9_f69OdrkQ1WYe4mhR8zE6j8pqqvfiEv75fa06YbXKibxu035E3MvF4OJ7pQi0XRJQY8G85LV_fYh6AdlUZqE6XTZJuvgDKDlgdRCOgO9ZDSAJz_-ew8=)\n[3] [math.rs](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG7S-PYA9cfmMRG8JAgSoy9_f69OdrkQ1WYe4mhR8zE6j8pqqvfiE